From ecda02a63caae2c097adfed5be65db6b737c36e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Amaan Javed <68250881+amaanJvd@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 09:06:14 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(qa): forward configured base_url to QA analysis LLM
 (#527) (#613)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

* fix(qa): forward configured base_url to QA analysis LLM (#527)

QA analysis dropped the LLM base_url for the openai provider, so a config
pointing at an OpenAI-compatible endpoint (xAI/grok, a local LLM, a proxy)
sent QA requests to OpenAI's default endpoint and failed with 401 — even
though the conversation path honors base_url and works. Root cause:
resolve_user_llm_config only forwarded base_url for the openrouter provider.

Forward base_url for any non-azure provider (matching the conversation
path), and mirror it in the QA-node own-LLM path by treating qa_endpoint as
an OpenAI-compatible base_url for non-azure providers. Adds regression tests
for both paths.

Fixes #527

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* refactor(qa): scope base_url fix to the workflow-LLM path (#527)

Address review (cubic P2): the QA-node own-LLM path reused qa_endpoint as an
OpenAI-compatible base_url, but qa_endpoint is Azure-only in the UI, so
non-azure QA-node users can't populate it — the branch was unreachable.
Drop that half-wired path and keep the core, reported, UI-reachable fix
(resolve_user_llm_config forwarding base_url for non-azure). Proper QA-node
custom-endpoint support needs a dedicated qa_base_url field + UI (follow-up).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* fix(qa): centralize LLM service creation

